      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From an urban planning perspective, high-density housing is often touted as vital for combating sprawl, supporting walkable communities, and improving resource efficiency. Economically, density can support robust local businesses and maximize land use value within city limits. However, the \"consensus\" is rarely absolute; challenges like adequate transit provision and affordable unit mix must also be demonstrably addressed for such growth to be truly beneficial. True progressive planning requires balancing growth potential with localized quality-of-life needs.",
